            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "test/unpack_properties.cpp",
                    "line": 186,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why wouldn't this be:  `ASSERT_TRUE(error.has_value())`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/unpack_properties.cpp",
                    "line": 186,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Use explicit control\u2011flow guards (if (opt) { use(*opt); } / if (!opt) return;) because clang\u2011tidy doesn\u2019t treat test macros (ASSERT_TRUE, EXPECT_TRUE) as flow\u2011stopping\u2014so keep assertions for tests, .Use EXPECT_TRUE(error.has_value()) plus if (!ctx) return; to avoid duplication while keeping failures visible and the optional access analyzable."
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/unpack_properties.cpp",
                    "line": 186,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/unpack_properties.cpp",
                    "line": 254,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Just make this one an ASSERT."
